 "narrative": [
  "Joint Major in Mathematics and Economics (MA33 in the mathematics department and EN28 in the economics department); also described on the Economics page (https://catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/ECON-ug.html).",
  "Economics page differences: ODE listed as MATH 130; MATH 109 substitution for students completing MATH 31CH; last group lists ECON 172A-B or ECON 171 and ECON 172A; 'a minimum of seven courses from one department and eight from the other', chosen from the courses listed.",
  "A total of fifteen upper-division courses (totaling sixty units) are required (with a minimum of seven courses from each department—mathematics and economics).",
  "All majors must obtain a minimum 2.0 grade point average in the upper-division courses used to satisfy the major requirements. The student must receive a grade of C– or better in any course to be counted toward fulfillment of the major requirements. All courses used to fulfill the major must be taken for a letter grade.",
  "No more than three upper-division courses taken externally from UC San Diego can be counted toward the major.",
  "MATH 195, 196, 197, 198, 199, and 199H cannot be used toward any mathematics major.",
  "Students in the joint major cannot double major with any other major in the mathematics or economics departments, and cannot minor in mathematics or economics.",
  "Strongly recommended (not required): MATH 193A-B and 194 and ECON 109, 113, 175, and 178 (Economics page: MATH 190, 193A-B and ECON 109, 113, 173A-B, 174, 178; MATH 142 recommended over MATH 140)."
